yo-minus-freezer differences, exactly one per accession, so no repeated measurements from the same independent unit enter a row-independent procedure as if independent.\",\"The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue: it states 16 independent units and 16 rows analysed with exactly one row per accession, and explicitly notes that no accession contributes more than one row and that the 16 differences entering the test are the 16 independent observations the design provides.\",\"Report figures reproduce from data/input.csv (mean difference 8.00 pp, SD 6.00, SE 1.50, t(15) = 5.333, 95% CI 4.80 to 11.20, Cohen's dz 1.33, min/max gains 1 and 19 pp, freezer range 29 to 66%), confirming the selected result reflects the accession-level paired analysis described.\",\"No minted authority lock is present, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column accession_id is consistent with the frozen data: all 16 rows carry distinct accession IDs (FSB-101 through FSB-116), and the workflow enforces uniqueness before analysis, so no unit is represented on more than one row.","Both procedure arms respect the unit structure: the paired t-test (stats.ttest_rel) and the Wilcoxon signed-rank check operate on the 16 within-row cryo-minus-freezer differences, exactly one per accession, so no repeated measurements from the same independent unit enter a row-independent procedure as if independent.","The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue: it states 16 independent units and 16 rows analysed with exactly one row per accession, and explicitly notes that no accession contributes more than one row and that the 16 differences entering the test are the 16 independent observations the design provides.","Report figures reproduce from data/input.csv (mean difference 8.00 pp, SD 6